course: dictionary
lesson: 9343
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must check the clues in the sentence to know which one the author means. Spirit is one of these words. «The Trinity means one God in three persons: the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit» uses spirit as part of a religious name, not as a ghost.
explain: Spirit can mean a ghost, as in «Stories and cartoons give us pictures, floating spirits». Here the clue is the word floating, which shows it is a ghost-like being. Other clues, like team or mood, point to other meanings.
explain: Spirit can also mean courage and energy: team spirit means a group working together with determination. In high spirits means happy. Read the words around the word and try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Words from real life carry meaning too. «Bon Odori is a calm circle dance at Japan's summer Obon festival, which honours the spirits of ancestors.» Ancestors are people who lived long ago, so spirits here means the spirits of those people. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Spirit is a noun, so it can name a thing, such as a ghost or a feeling.
fact: Spirit can also be a verb: «spirit away» means take someone or something away secretly.
fact: «Team spirit» means courage, energy and determination shared by a group.
fact: «In good spirits» or «in high spirits» means happy.
fact: Spirit can mean the real purpose of a rule, as in «the spirit of the law».
exercise: «Bon Odori honours the spirits of ancestors.» What are the spirits here? | Clouds in the sky | Toys that float on water | *The spirits of people who lived long ago | Dancers in costumes
exercise: Mia says the team has great spirit before the match. What does spirit mean? | An empty, quiet field | A glass of strong drink | *Courage and energy to keep going together | A small fish in a pond
exercise: Gran says the boys were in high spirits at the party. What does that mean? | Angry and loud | Ill and tired | *Happy | Asleep
test: «Stories and cartoons give us floating spirits.» Here spirits means | Small fish in a pond | *Ghosts or magical beings | Empty bottles | Clouds of smoke
test: Lena cheers, «That's the spirit!» after a brave try. What does she mean? | Go away | Please be quiet | Stop trying now | *Well done, keep your energy and courage up
exam: The referee kept to the spirit of the rule, not just its exact words. What does spirit mean here? | A ghost in the stadium | Strong drink for the crowd | *The real purpose or meaning of the rule | Ink for the scoreboard
